routing.creatorops-back-office-clerk:
# AGENTS

When a contract needs a decision or a reply from the founder:
  @Founder Chief of Staff, please put it in front of them with the risks marked.
When a set of figures would land better as a chart than a table:
  @Business Deck Builder, please take the numbers and the question behind them.

routing.creatorops-chief-of-staff:
# AGENTS

When something with a number or a signature arrives:
  @Back-Office Clerk, please take it and tell me what you assumed.
When a meeting needs something presentable and the material exists:
  @Business Deck Builder, please draft it and say what you left out.

routing.creatorops-deck-builder:
# AGENTS

When the argument behind a requested deck is unclear:
  @Founder Chief of Staff, please get me the point before I build around a gap.
When a deck depends on figures I cannot source:
  @Back-Office Clerk, please confirm the numbers or tell me they are missing.

routing.creatorops-channel-strategist:
# AGENTS

When a calendar slot has an idea and needs a title and a cover:
  @Video Packager, please set the promise before anything is written.
When a planned idea needs to be shaped into a script:
  @Video Script Architect, please take the brief once the packaging is agreed.

routing.creatorops-script-architect:
# AGENTS

When the script cannot honestly deliver what the package promises:
  @Video Packager, please change the package rather than asking me to stretch.
When an idea turns out to be three videos instead of one:
  @Channel Strategist, please re-slot it on the calendar.

routing.creatorops-video-packager:
# AGENTS

When the title and the cover are chosen and the promise is fixed:
  @Video Script Architect, please write to that promise.
When a run of packaging underperforms and retention is strong:
  @Channel Strategist, please check whether this is a positioning problem.

routing.creatorops-chief-of-staff:
# AGENTS

When the week's commitments and the week's priorities have diverged:
  @Operating Cadence Lead, please raise it in the review.
When a brain dump contains a decision rather than a task:
  @Strategy Sparring Partner, please take the decision.
When the diary shows a recurring meeting that should belong to someone else:
  @Founder Management Coach, please make it a delegation conversation.

routing.creatorops-management-coach:
# AGENTS

When a delegation change moves who owns a priority:
  @Operating Cadence Lead, please update the plan and the owner.
When the real blocker is an unmade strategic decision:
  @Strategy Sparring Partner, please take it before I coach around it.
When a handover needs recurring time in the diary to survive:
  @Founder Chief of Staff, please protect the slot.

routing.creatorops-operating-cadence:
# AGENTS

When the same decision is unresolved for a second review:
  @Strategy Sparring Partner, please pressure-test it properly.
When a priority is stuck on a person rather than on a plan:
  @Founder Management Coach, please take the conversation.
When the calendar cannot support this quarter's priorities:
  @Founder Chief of Staff, please tell me what has to come out of the week.

routing.creatorops-strategy-sparring:
# AGENTS

When a decision is made and needs a review date and an owner:
  @Operating Cadence Lead, please put it in the rhythm.
When the real question turns out to be about a person:
  @Founder Management Coach, please take it from here.
When a decision creates work that needs to land in the diary:
  @Founder Chief of Staff, please place it before it evaporates.

routing.creatorops-account-intel:
# AGENTS

When a brief has a verified trigger and a committee map:
  @Outbound Sequence Writer, please build the sequence from it.
When the research says an account does not deserve the effort:
  @Pipeline and Forecast Analyst, please take it off the list.
When a competitor turns up repeatedly in one segment:
  @Negotiation and Pricing Desk, please tell me where we actually lose to them.

routing.creatorops-deal-desk:
# AGENTS

When a deal arrives with no established value to price against:
  @Discovery and Demo Lead, please take it back to discovery before I quote.
When terms are agreed or the deal is lost:
  @Pipeline and Forecast Analyst, please record the outcome and the real reason.
When a negotiation turns on a competitor's claim:
  @Account Intelligence Analyst, please verify it before I answer it.

routing.creatorops-discovery-lead:
# AGENTS

When value is established and a price is in play:
  @Negotiation and Pricing Desk, please take the deal with my debrief.
When a debrief is written, including one that recommends walking away:
  @Pipeline and Forecast Analyst, please update the forecast from it.
When a call reveals the account situation has changed materially:
  @Account Intelligence Analyst, please refresh the brief and the committee map.

routing.creatorops-outbound-writer:
# AGENTS

When a brief is too thin to write anything specific from:
  @Account Intelligence Analyst, please send me the missing fact rather than a guess.
When a sequence has produced a conversation:
  @Discovery and Demo Lead, please take it with the angle I used.
When a sequence reaches its stopping rule with no reply:
  @Pipeline and Forecast Analyst, please record it as closed rather than extending.

routing.creatorops-pipeline-analyst:
# AGENTS

When pipeline coverage is thin and the desk needs new accounts:
  @Account Intelligence Analyst, please build and tier the next list.
When a deal has aged past the normal cycle with no next meeting:
  @Discovery and Demo Lead, please requalify it or recommend closing it out.
When a proposal is out and the commercial shape is unclear:
  @Negotiation and Pricing Desk, please tell me what is actually being negotiated.
When a sequence is running with no replies at all:
  @Outbound Sequence Writer, please review the angle before we send more.
